course: dictionary
lesson: 6054
title: Mention: a short reference
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To mention something is to say or write about it briefly, without many details. A mention is that short reference itself. «At the party, nobody mentions the broken vase, so they just carry on talking.» The word mentions shows the vase is spoken about only in passing.
explain: Use the words around mention to work out its meaning. «Hana tells her mum that Chloe's parents are splitting up; her mum mentions it at the school gate, and soon the news has spread.» Mentions it means brings it up briefly. Try your meaning in the sentence: "her mum brings it up at the school gate" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Mention also has a polite use. When someone says «Thank you», you can reply «Don't mention it», which means "you're welcome". In reading questions you may be asked, «What is mentioned in paragraph 2?» Look for the brief references in the text, not just the long details.
fact: To mention something means to say or write about it briefly, without lots of details.
fact: A mention is a short reference to someone or something.
fact: «Don't mention it» is a polite reply to «thank you», and it means you're welcome.
fact: An «honourable mention» is praise for doing well, even though you did not win.
fact: Useful phrases: «mention something to someone», «not to mention» (meaning and also), and «as mentioned» (meaning as said before).
exercise: «Her mum mentions it at the school gate.» What does mentions mean here? | Shouts about it loudly for everyone to hear | Writes a long book about it | *Says something about it briefly | Hides it from everyone
exercise: Ben says «Thanks for lending me your pen!» You reply, «Don't mention it.» What does it mean? | *You're welcome | Give it back now | Please never talk about this again | I forgot the pen
exercise: «The book got a mention on the radio.» What is a mention in this sentence? | *A short reference to the book | A long review of the radio | A new book for sale | A prize for winning a competition
test: «They stand round the trampoline until someone mentions the new map.» What is mentioned? | *The new map | The birthday cake | The trampoline | Their trainers
test: «The hotel was clean, not to mention cheap.» What does not to mention mean here? | Forget to say | *And also | Except for the cheap part | Without saying anything at all
exam: «Some doubted his story because he did not mention the Great Wall or tea.» What does did not mention mean? | Went to visit them | *Did not say anything about them | Bought them to take home | Drew pictures of them
